WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.360
The small intestine presents
an extensive epithelial surface to

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:03.976
the lumen.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:08.190
These projecting villi provide
the geometry needed to understand

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.656
the course packet’s celiac disease explanation.

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:15.087
In the supplied mechanism,
gluten ingestion triggers immune injury

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.658
to the villous epithelium.

00:00:17.280 --> 00:00:20.871
T-cell infiltration accompanies
inflammation and mucosal destruction.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.126
Watch the projections shorten and flatten.

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.550
The loss of surface
connects tissue injury with impaired

00:00:27.580 --> 00:00:27.830
absorption.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:31.100
The packet calls for permanent gluten exclusion.

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:35.074
It separately permits lactose
reintroduction after villous healing.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:39.350
These are different instructions:
recovery does not end gluten

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:39.724
avoidance.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:43.690
This schematic deformation shows
a mechanism, not a measured

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:45.823
healing time or a diagnostic biopsy.
